<title>UK: Wembley U.S. firm faces $22.75 mln damages.</title>
<headline>Wembley U.S. firm faces $22.75 mln damages.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Wembley Plc said on Thursday that one of its U.S. subsidiaries, PCC Management Inc, faced damages worth $22.75 million in a court case brought against it by MovieFone Inc.  </p>
<p>Moviefone and PCC entered into a contract in 1992 but ran into conflict over subsequent business deals.</p>
<p>Moviefone launched $96 million arbitration proceedings on charges of profit losses incurred by it.</p>
<p>The legal costs to date incurred by Wembley are estimated to be two million stg out of which 1.25 million was provided in the group's 1996 accounts.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
